  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be rotated through a right angle about its line of intersection with the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. If the mirror image of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in the rotated plane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "fVp9f",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4jFZd",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "p1cTD",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
